    <bpmn:process id="W_W4122" name="W4122. Network Modeling, Scenario Simulation &amp; What-If Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Network decision; growth; disruption; what-if question
Frequency: Continuous + per decision
Volume: Enterprise network models (DC/store/lane/inventory)
Owner: Network Strategy Lead / Supply Chain Analytics (VS-28)
Participants: Analytics (VS-28), Supply Planning (VS-02), Finance (VS-17.4), Real Estate (VS-97)
Source: workflow W4122 — Network Modeling, Scenario Simulation &amp; What-If Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4122_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4122_Lane1" name="Network Strategy Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4122_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4122_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4122_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4122_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4122_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4122_Start3" name="Network decision; growth; disruption; what-if question">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4122_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4122_Task4" name="Network Strategy/Analytics build and maintain the network model (demand by…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Network Strategy/Analytics build and maintain the network model (demand by location, DC/store nodes, lanes, lead times, cost, capacity, inventory) fed by demand planning (VS-127/VS-02) and master data (VS-29)
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Analytics
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4122_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4122_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4122_Task5" name="Network Strategy run scenarios (new DC, DC closure, store growth, port change…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Network Strategy run scenarios (new DC, DC closure, store growth, port change, modal shift, service-level change), and quantify cost/service/working-capital impact
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4122_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4122_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4122_Task6" name="Network Strategy present scenario results, recommend, and feed decisions into…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Network Strategy present scenario results, recommend, and feed decisions into network design (W4123–W4127) and business cases (W4128)
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4122_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4122_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4122_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4122_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4122_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-638 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Network Strategy, Modeling &amp; Design (PA-136.1).) | - CTL-638: model assumptions documented and validated; results reviewed by Finance/SC leadership
Owner: Network Strategy Lead / Supply Chain Analytics (VS-28)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4122_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4122_Annotation8" targetRef="W4122_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
